                'Warming waters are shifting the distribution of prey and of the animals that depend on it, and loss of sea ice is removing the hunting platform of polar bears and resting places for walruses and ice seals. Marine heatwaves have triggered harmful algal blooms that poison sea lions, and disease outbreaks can be devastating: phocine distemper killed tens of thousands of harbour seals in the North Sea in 1988 and 2002, and, from 2022, highly pathogenic H5N1 avian influenza killed tens of thousands of sea lions and elephant seals in South America.',
